%% title: Which scale applies to which results
%% desc: Each academic year has one scale for all classes. If a class has its own scale, that one applies to that class. When results are processed, the percentage is rounded to a whole number and matched to a grade row.
flowchart LR
  Y["Academic year"]:::admin --> A["All-classes<br/>scale"]:::admin
  Y --> C["A class's<br/>own scale"]:::admin
  A --> Q{"Does the class have<br/>its own scale?"}:::note
  C --> Q
  Q -->|"Yes"| CU["That one applies"]
  Q -->|"No"| AU["The all-classes<br/>scale applies"]
  CU --> R["Result processing:<br/>percentage to grade and GPA"]:::guardian
  AU --> R
  classDef teacher fill:#e7f5ff,stroke:#1c7ed6,color:#0b3d66
  classDef admin fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#e8590c,color:#7a2e05
  classDef guardian fill:#ebfbee,stroke:#2b8a3e,color:#14411d
  classDef note fill:#f1f3f5,stroke:#868e96,color:#343a40
